---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
	title="Privacy"
	description="bechdel.io counts visits with Plausible: no cookies, no personal data, nothing sold or shared. Here's exactly what's collected."
	nav="privacy"
>
	<div class="page">
		<h1 class="page-title">Privacy</h1>
		<p class="page-lead">We count visits so we know which films people read about. We don't track you.</p>

		<div class="prose">
			<h2>What we collect</h2>
			<p>
				We use <a href="https://plausible.io/data-policy" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Plausible</a>, an analytics tool
				that doesn't use cookies and doesn't collect personal data. We run our own copy of it, so the numbers stay with us. For each
				visit it records:
			</p>
			<ul>
				<li>the page you opened and the page that sent you here</li>
				<li>your country, browser, operating system and whether you're on a phone</li>
				<li>which outside links you follow, like IMDb or GitHub</li>
				<li>broken links and errors on the site, so we can fix them</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				Plausible doesn't store your IP address. It can't follow you across sites or link one visit to the next day's. Nothing is
				sold or shared. Visits from bots aren't counted.
			</p>

			<h2>Hosting</h2>
			<p>
				The site is hosted on GitHub Pages. GitHub may log your IP address when it serves a page, for security; see
				<a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">GitHub's privacy statement</a>.
			</p>
			<p>
				Film posters and stills load from The Movie Database (TMDB), so TMDB sees your IP address when your browser fetches them; see
				<a href="https://www.themoviedb.org/privacy-policy" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">TMDB's privacy policy</a>.
			</p>

			<h2>What we don't do</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>No cookies, no accounts, no forms</li>
				<li>No ads and no ad trackers</li>
				<li>No fonts or scripts loaded from other companies. Everything but the posters and stills comes from this site, and the analytics come from our own server.</li>
			</ul>

			<h2>Questions</h2>
			<p>
				<a href="https://github.com/JoeKarlsson/bechdel-test/issues" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Open an issue on GitHub</a>
				and we'll answer.
			</p>
			<p class="note">Last updated 12 November 2026</p>
		</div>
	</div>
</Base>
